@* The application's version, centred at the foot of every page.

   None of the four designs draws a footer, so this is a deliberate addition to them, recorded here
   rather than silently. Its styling is the header's instead of a new vocabulary - the same
   --surface, --on-surface-variant and label-sm - so the two ends of a page read as a pair.

   On the builder there is a pinned 320px panel over the left of the window, and the version there
   is centred on the content column rather than the window. That is a rule in base.css which
   follows the panel itself, because the store page shares the builder's layout without having a
   panel. *@
<footer class="app-footer" aria-label="Version">
    <div class="container app-footer__inner">
        <span class="app-footer__version">@AppVersion.Current</span>
    </div>
</footer>
